+# PLAN — ACP Subagent Grouping & Virtual Transcripts
+
+Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-23-acp-subagent-grouping-design.md`
+Branch: `feature/acp-subagent-grouping` (off `zedium-applied`)
+Started: 2026-06-23 22:38 MSK
+
+## Vision
+
+External ACP providers (qwen-code first) currently dump subagent steps flat into the main
+transcript with no separate-transcript affordance. Generalize Zed-native's
+card+live-preview+pop-out subagent UX to any ACP provider via:
+- a `SubagentGrouping` trait with per-provider adapters (Native + Qwen),
+- a normalized `SubagentIndex` membership model on `AcpThread`,
+- ingest wiring that classifies tool calls from their raw `acp::ToolCall` `_meta`,
+- generalized rendering (skip members in main list; card for roots) + a read-only
+  recursive virtual sub-transcript for pop-out.
+
+Two wire shapes must both normalize: native = separate session + `subagent_session_info`
+index range; qwen = single session + flat tool calls tagged `parentToolCallId` /
+`provenance:"subagent"` / `subagentType`.
+
+## Milestones (dependency-ordered)
+
+- **M0 — Baseline green.** `cargo check -p acp_thread` passes on the starting tree.
+  STATUS: IN-PROGRESS (background build)
+
+- **M1 — Normalized model.** `SubagentMembership`, `SubagentGroup`, `SubagentIndex`
+  (roots IndexMap, membership map, `is_subagent_root`/`membership_of`/`subtree_entries`),
+  and the `SubagentGrouping` trait, all in `acp_thread`. Pure data + queries, no provider
+  logic, no UI. Unit tests for the index/tree queries.
+  VERIFY: `cargo test -p acp_thread`. STATUS: TODO
+
+- **M2 — Adapters.** `QwenSubagentGrouping` (`_meta.parentToolCallId`/`provenance`/
+  `subagentType`, root = `toolName=="agent"`) and `NativeSubagentGrouping`
+  (`subagent_session_info`). Unit tests driven by the live qwen wire capture distilled to
+  a JSONL fixture + a synthetic nested case + a native case.
+  VERIFY: `cargo test -p acp_thread`. STATUS: TODO
+
+- **M3 — Ingest + seam.** `AgentConnection::subagent_grouping() -> Option<Rc<dyn ...>>`
+  (default None). Wire classify into `handle_session_update` (operate on raw `acp::ToolCall`
+  where full `_meta` is present). Maintain the index; lazy/out-of-order resolution; orphan
+  fallback; no-adapter no-op. Ingest tests.
+  VERIFY: `cargo test -p acp_thread`. STATUS: TODO
+
+- **M4 — Adapter selection.** `AcpConnection` (agent_servers) returns an adapter chosen
+  from `agentInfo.name` ("qwen-code" → Qwen). `NativeAgentConnection` returns Native.
+  VERIFY: `cargo check -p agent_servers` (+ targeted test if cheap). STATUS: TODO
+
+- **M5 — Rendering: card + member-skip.** Generalize `render_subagent_card` to be driven by
+  `SubagentIndex`; skip member tool calls in the main flat list; card shows type/status/
+  count/summary + live preview. agent_ui (slow build, higher risk).
+  VERIFY: `cargo check -p agent_ui` + existing agent_ui tests. STATUS: TODO
+
+- **M6 — Virtual recursive pop-out.** Read-only `SubagentView` over `subtree_entries(root)`
+  reusing `ThreadView::render_entry`; recursive nested cards + breadcrumb back via existing
+  `navigate_to_thread` substrate. agent_ui (slow, highest risk).
+  VERIFY: `cargo check -p agent_ui`. STATUS: TODO
+
+## Strategy / risk notes
+
+- M1–M3 live in the fast `acp_thread` crate and are high-confidence + heavily unit-tested.
+  Land these rock-solid and committed first — that is real, defensible value even if UI
+  slips.
+- M4 medium. M5–M6 touch `thread_view.rs` (~10k lines), slow to compile, highest risk.
+  If they can't go green honestly tonight, leave BLOCKED with the model layer fully landed.
+- thread_view.rs is one giant file → M5/M6 serialize (no parallel edits to same file).
+- Decision (reversible, low blast radius): membership stored in a side-index on AcpThread
+  keyed by ToolCallId rather than widening `ToolCall`. Keeps non-subagent providers
+  untouched.
+- Classify runs on the raw `acp::ToolCall` at ingest because Zed's converted `ToolCall`
+  does not retain arbitrary `_meta` (only specific keys). This is why the trait takes
+  `&acp::ToolCall`.
